(Malware detection models are usually trained on fixed datasets and updated when new malware types) Tj
T* (appear. During such updates, models often forget previously learned malware patterns, a problem) Tj
T* (known as catastrophic forgetting. Retraining models using all old and new data is not practical due to) Tj
T* (large data size and storage limitations. This propses to address this issue by using a GAN-based) Tj
T* (generative replay approach, where synthetic malware samples are generated to represent older) Tj
T* (malware classes. These generated samples are combined with new malware data during training to) Tj
T* (help the model retain past knowledge. The effectiveness of this approach is evaluated by comparing) Tj
T* (detection accuracy before and after learning new malware classes.) Tj
T* (To overcome  hardware and other resources constraints, the original MalCL framework can be) Tj
T* (downsized by using a smaller subset of the dataset, fewer malware classes, and reduced training) Tj
T* (epochs preserving the core generative replay mechanism while ensuring feasible execution on) Tj
T* (moderate resouces such as laptop.) Tj
