(Large Language Models \(LLMs\) are widely used today, but they often give answers that sound) Tj
T* (confident even when they are wrong. These mistakes, called hallucinations, can be risky when AI is) Tj
T* (used for learning, healthcare, or decision-making. This project focuses on detecting such) Tj
T* (hallucinations by looking inside the model, instead of only checking its final answers. By studying the) Tj
T* (␀m␀o␀d␀e␀lÿý␀s␀ ␀i␀n␀t␀e␀r␀n␀a␀l␀ ␀r␀e␀p␀r␀e␀s␀e␀n␀t␀a␀t␀i␀o␀n␀s␀ ␀w␀h␀i␀l␀e␀ ␀i␀t␀ ␀g␀e␀n␀e␀r␀a␀t␀e␀s␀ ␀m␀u␀l␀t␀i␀p␀l␀e␀ ␀r␀e␀s␀p␀o␀n␀s␀e␀s␀,␀ ␀w␀e␀ ␀c␀a␀n␀ ␀m␀e␀a␀s␀u␀r␀e␀ ␀h␀o␀w) Tj
T* (consistent or uncertain its understanding really is. This approach helps identify both confused and) Tj
T* (overconfident wrong answers, making AI systems safer, more reliable, and easier to trust.) Tj
