(Generating crystal structures directly from textual descriptions marks a pivotal advancement in) Tj
T* (materials informatics, offering a streamlined pathway from concept to discovery. Integrating) Tj
T* (generative models into Crystal Structure Prediction \(CSP\) presents a transformative) Tj
T* (opportunity) Tj
T* (to enhance efficiency and innovation. While large language models \(LLMs\) excel at) Tj
T* (understanding) Tj
T* (and generating text, their potential in materials discovery remains largely unexplored. Here,) Tj
T* (we) Tj
T* (introduce CrysText, an advanced approach for generating crystal structures from simple text) Tj
T* (prompts, conditioned on material composition and space group number. Leveraging) Tj
T* (Llama-3.1-) Tj
T* (8B fine-tuned with Quantized Low-Rank Adaptation \(QLoRA\), our approach enables the) Tj
T* (efficient) Tj
T* (and scalable generation of CIF-formatted structures directly from input descriptions,) Tj
T* (eliminating) Tj
T* (the need for post-processing and ensuring effective fine-tuning with rapid inference.) Tj
T* (Evaluations) Tj
T* (on the MP-20 benchmark dataset demonstrate high structure match rates and effective RMSE) Tj
T* (metrics, showcasing the framework's ability to generate crystal structures that faithfully adhere) Tj
T* (to) Tj
T* (specified compositions and crystal symmetries. By conditioning on energy above the hull, we) Tj
T* (further demonstrate the potential of CrysText to generate stable crystal structures. Our work) Tj
T* (highlights the transformative role of LLMs in text-prompted inverse design, accelerating the) Tj
T* (discovery of new materials.) Tj
